course: dictionary
lesson: 13328
title: Guava: a tropical fruit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A guava is a fruit that grows in hot, wet countries. The word can also mean the small tree that the fruit grows on. Read the words around guava to find out which meaning fits. «Mum cut a ripe guava in half and shared it.» You can eat it, so here guava means the fruit.
explain: «The guava tree in the garden was tall and full of fruit.» The word tree is the clue. The guava is the plant, not the food. One word can have two meanings, so always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Sometimes the words around a word tell you where something is found. «In India, the sweet guavas were sold at every market.» India is a hot country, so this sentence helps you guess that guavas grow in warm places.
fact: A guava is a tropical fruit that is round or pear-shaped, with green or yellow skin.
fact: Inside a guava, the flesh is pink or white and sweet, and it has many small seeds.
fact: The guava tree is a small tree that grows the fruit.
fact: Guavas are rich in vitamin C, which helps keep your body healthy.
fact: Guavas grow in hot countries such as India, Africa and the Caribbean.
exercise: «The children ate a ripe guava after lunch.» What is a guava in this sentence? | *A tropical fruit | A tall, cold mountain | A type of bird | A hot sandy beach
exercise: «The guava tree in the garden was covered in green fruit.» What does guava mean here? | A large bag of seeds | A cool breeze from the sea | *The small tree that the fruit grows on | A pink sweet drink
exercise: «Inside the guava, the flesh was pink and sweet.» What colour was the flesh? | Black | Purple with yellow spots | Blue | *Pink
test: «Guavas are rich in vitamin C.» What does this tell you about guavas? | They can fly like birds | They are made of metal | *They are good for your health | They are very cold to touch
test: Where do guavas grow? | *In hot countries such as India | Inside a fridge | Deep under the sea | At the top of the highest mountain in the snow
exam: Sara says, «The guava is round, with green skin.» What shape is a guava? | Square | Triangle | *Round | Flat like a leaf
